      "field": "/description",
      "text": "Literal printed masses and added distilled-water volume per source preparation. G/MG_PER_PREPARATION_WITH_1_L_WATER describes a recipe batch containing1L added water, not a final1L solution or final concentration. NBRC1020 and JCM317 have the same nominal listed masses (4 mg sodium selenite and 4 mg tungstate reagent) plus 1 L distilled water, but NBRC1020 omits hydrate qualifiers while JCM317 explicitly states Na2WO4·2H2O. Omission establishes neither anhydrous identity nor equality/difference. Keep these source-bound partial proposals; do not merge or co-install them as proved-distinct owners without source-applicable supplied-reagent evidence or an explicitly reviewed common nominal scope. The 1 L is added water, not a demonstrated final solution volume.",
